{"id": "features-wide", "window": ["2016-10-24", "2022-12-30"], "cells_tested": 614, "cells_pass_bh": 189, "cells_expected_by_chance": 18.9, "cells_note": "cells_expected_by_chance = q x passes (expected false discoveries). Raw p<0.05: 200 vs 30.7 by chance. 92 passes are net-R-below-zero cells (the spread). Cells leaning on the turbulent regime (2 episodes) are set to p = 1.", "intro": ["1,584 London sessions (2016-10-24 to 2022-12-30), 7 USD majors on the 1-minute bid/ask grid of stage 2; dollar = the other six majors (leave-own-out), β from the prior 20 sessions only. 2023 onwards is not looked at.", "The dollar share holds across every slice for every pair (all far above the 0.5% a wrong-day dollar explains), but its SIZE moves with the clock: it peaks in the 13:00-16:00 London overlap (EURUSD 62%, AUDUSD 67%, NZDUSD 69%, USDJPY 33%) and is lowest in Asia (USDJPY 12%). USDCAD is the exception: its own news lands at 13:30 with the US data, so its dollar share is highest in Asia and the London open (46%) and falls to 34% in the overlap.", "It rises with vol: the high-σ third has 9-19 points more dollar share than the low third in five of seven pairs, and 2021-2022 is the most dollar-driven stretch (GBPUSD 19% in 2019 to 56% in 2022; USDJPY 34% in 2017 to 7% in 2019, back to 27% in 2022). The turbulent regime looks higher still, but C.OG's rule finds only 2 turbulent episodes in the window (Apr-Aug 2020, Jun-Dec 2022), so regime is too noisy to tell apart from year.", "THE MARKET QUESTION: a dollar-led big 15-minute move and an own-led one behave the same. Pooled, the follow-through difference is -0.001σ at 1h and -0.010σ to 22:00, against a 0.037σ (1h) to 0.085σ (22:00) round trip; stop-through beyond 0.25σ is 58.4% vs 58.5%. It is not a plateau: 0 of 27 neighbouring settings pass, and the sign flips between them.", "The only local pattern: own-led moves in the NY afternoon (16-22 London) give back 0.008σ in 15 minutes and 0.025σ by 22:00, while dollar-led ones do not (difference +0.030σ). As a trade it loses: fading them at a 0.25σ stop/target is about +0.06R gross and negative net once one spread (≈0.15R) is paid.", "Forbes-Rigobon: raw correlation of the majors rises from 0.40 on the calmest tenth of days to 0.50-0.54 on the loudest, but corrected for the louder variance it FALLS (0.40 to 0.23 in the top decile): loud days are louder own moves, not a dollar that takes over. Sorted on yesterday's vol the corrected line is flat to falling too (0.41 to 0.32).", "The 7-major absorption ratio (top PC share, rolling 63 sessions) runs 0.36-0.74, mean 0.56 vs 0.15 for shuffled re-pairings; it bottomed on 2020-03-11 (the COVID dash split yen, franc and commodity currencies) and ended 2022 at its high, 0.74. Top-2 PCs take 0.71.", "Tail risk: the dollar's worst days and a pair's own worst days mostly come apart, as under shuffling, except USDCAD (12 joint top-5% days vs 3.8 shuffled) and GBPUSD same-direction (7 vs 1.8): for those two a dollar shock and an own shock tend to land together, so a hedge built from the dollar factor leaves the tail in.", "What it means: the split is a RISK description (where the variance comes from, by hour and by year), not an entry signal. Size books on the dollar share of the hour; do not expect a stop to behave differently because the move that hit it was dollar or own.", "Sweep: 614 cells tested; 189 pass Benjamini-Hochberg at q = 0.10 (about 18.9 of those expected false). 92 of the passes are just 'net R is below 0' (the spread), so the informative passes are 97: almost all are the dollar-share-by-hour/year/σ cells; of 96 dollar-minus-own follow cells, 4 pass."], "holds": [{"effect": "Dollar share of variance depends on the hour", "where": "every pair; peak 13-16 London (EURUSD 0.62, AUDUSD 0.67, USDJPY 0.33), low in Asia (USDJPY 0.12); USDCAD reversed (0.46 Asia/London open, 0.34 overlap)", "size": "12-21 points between buckets", "benchmark": "pair's pooled share; wrong-day dollar < 0.01"}, {"effect": "Dollar share rises with σ", "where": "5 of 7 pairs (AUD, NZD, CAD, CHF, JPY; EURUSD +6 and GBPUSD +3 do not pass): high-σ third minus low third", "size": "+9 to +19 points", "benchmark": "low-σ third; wrong-day dollar < 0.01"}, {"effect": "Dollar share drifts by year", "where": "all; 2019 lowest, 2021-22 highest (GBPUSD 0.19 to 0.56, USDCAD 0.19 to 0.54)", "size": "up to 37 points", "benchmark": "pooled share"}, {"effect": "Dollar-led vs own-led big moves: no difference", "where": "holds across pairs, hours, σ thirds, years; 27 neighbouring settings; +1 lag", "size": "-0.001σ at 1h, -0.010σ to 22:00; stop-through 58.4% vs 58.5%", "benchmark": "0, all-big-moves pool, round trip 0.037-0.085σ"}, {"effect": "Own-led moves give back a little in the NY afternoon", "where": "local to 16-22 London", "size": "-0.025σ to 22:00 (dollar-led minus own +0.030σ); fade ≈ +0.06R gross, negative net", "benchmark": "0 and one spread (~0.15R)"}, {"effect": "Forbes-Rigobon-corrected correlation does not rise with vol", "where": "same-day vol deciles 6-10; yesterday-sorted too (not significant)", "size": "0.40 calm to 0.23 loudest decile (raw 0.50)", "benchmark": "calmest decile; forward heteroskedasticity map 0.70"}, {"effect": "Absorption ratio well above chance", "where": "all of 2017-2022", "size": "top-1 0.36-0.74 (mean 0.56), top-2 0.71", "benchmark": "shuffled 0.15 / 0.29"}, {"effect": "Joint worst days of dollar and own part", "where": "local to USDCAD and GBPUSD (same direction)", "size": "USDCAD 12 vs 3.8 days, GBPUSD 7 vs 1.8", "benchmark": "2,000 shuffled re-pairings"}], "charts": [{"type": "lines", "title": "Dollar share of 5-minute variance by London time of day", "unit": "share of variance", "xlabel": "1 Asia 00-07 · 2 London open 07-10 · 3 London mid 10-13 · 4 Overlap 13-16 · 5 NY afternoon 16-22", "note": "Each pair's share peaks in the 13:00-16:00 overlap, when US data lands, except USDCAD, whose own data lands at the same time. The other pairs, Asia to NY: AUDUSD 0.46/0.58/0.54/0.67/0.62; NZDUSD 0.46/0.58/0.53/0.69/0.59; USDCHF 0.35/0.33/0.35/0.51/0.48. Benchmark: a dollar path from a random other session explains under 0.01 in every bucket.", "series": [{"name": "EURUSD", "points": [[1, 0.4904], [2, 0.5169], [3, 0.4831], [4, 0.62], [5, 0.6121]]}, {"name": "GBPUSD", "points": [[1, 0.3992], [2, 0.3571], [3, 0.2904], [4, 0.471], [5, 0.4266]]}, {"name": "USDCAD", "points": [[1, 0.4604], [2, 0.463], [3, 0.3391], [4, 0.34], [5, 0.3528]]}, {"name": "USDJPY", "points": [[1, 0.1197], [2, 0.1548], [3, 0.1614], [4, 0.3299], [5, 0.2641]]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Dollar share by σ third (σ known at the open)", "names": ["Low σ third", "Mid σ third", "High σ third"], "unit": "share of 5-minute variance", "note": "Thirds of the layer-1 σ forecast, cut per pair over the window. Read across: in five of seven pairs the dollar takes 9-19 points more of the variance when σ is high (EURUSD +6, GBPUSD +3). Benchmark: the wrong-day dollar, under 0.01.", "rows": [{"label": "EURUSD", "values": [0.525, 0.5397, 0.5816]}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "values": [0.4034, 0.3162, 0.4314]}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "values": [0.4441, 0.5277, 0.6293]}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "values": [0.459, 0.5207, 0.6293]}, {"label": "USDCAD", "values": [0.2687, 0.342, 0.4301]}, {"label": "USDCHF", "values": [0.3632, 0.406, 0.4567]}, {"label": "USDJPY", "values": [0.1206, 0.164, 0.2534]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Dollar share, calm vs turbulent regime (C.OG Lesson 05)", "names": ["Calm", "Turbulent", "Wrong-day dollar (benchmark)"], "unit": "share of 5-minute variance", "note": "Turbulent = 63-session FX vol above 1.25x its rolling median for 21+ sessions, past data only: 251 sessions in only 2 episodes (2020-04-09 to 2020-08-24, 2022-06-01 to 2022-12-30) vs 12 calm episodes. Turbulent is higher for every pair, but two episodes are also the two most dollar-driven years, so this is not separable from year; the cells are shown, never counted as passes.", "rows": [{"label": "EURUSD", "values": [0.5263, 0.6518, -0.597]}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "values": [0.3257, 0.5616, -0.3713]}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "values": [0.5098, 0.7369, -0.5415]}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "values": [0.5128, 0.7191, -0.5467]}, {"label": "USDCAD", "values": [0.3223, 0.5513, -0.3873]}, {"label": "USDCHF", "values": [0.398, 0.5072, -0.4507]}, {"label": "USDJPY", "values": [0.1826, 0.3024, -0.207]}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Year by year: dollar share of 5-minute variance", "unit": "share of variance", "xlabel": "year", "note": "AUDUSD and NZDUSD track EURUSD (0.38-0.71); USDCHF stays 0.30-0.48. Benchmark: the pooled share (EURUSD 0.56, GBPUSD 0.40, USDCAD 0.37, USDJPY 0.22). Every pair dips in 2019 and climbs to its high in 2021-2022.", "series": [{"name": "EURUSD", "points": [[2017, 0.4947], [2018, 0.6006], [2019, 0.49], [2020, 0.5226], [2021, 0.611], [2022, 0.6104]]}, {"name": "GBPUSD", "points": [[2017, 0.2204], [2018, 0.3741], [2019, 0.192], [2020, 0.3922], [2021, 0.5058], [2022, 0.5576]]}, {"name": "USDCAD", "points": [[2017, 0.2493], [2018, 0.3311], [2019, 0.1874], [2020, 0.3659], [2021, 0.4606], [2022, 0.54]]}, {"name": "USDJPY", "points": [[2017, 0.3377], [2018, 0.1055], [2019, 0.0657], [2020, 0.0976], [2021, 0.1937], [2022, 0.2677]]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "THE QUESTION: after a big 15-minute move, does dollar-led behave differently from own-led?", "names": ["Dollar-led", "Own-led", "Round-trip spread (cost)"], "unit": "daily σ, signed with the move (+ = continues)", "note": "Big = |15-min move| above the 90th percentile of the prior 60 sessions. Dollar-led = β×dollar is ≥70% of the move's square and same sign (29,897 moves); own-led = ≤30% (49,556). Entry one minute after the move on the mid; the cost bar is the bid/ask round trip. Both lines sit at 0 against a cost 4-10x larger. All-big-moves benchmark: -0.0021σ at 1h.", "rows": [{"label": "15m", "values": [-0.0, -0.0011, 0.0367]}, {"label": "1h", "values": [-0.0015, -0.0009, 0.0365]}, {"label": "4h", "values": [-0.002, 0.0009, 0.0365]}, {"label": "rest", "values": [-0.0104, -0.0003, 0.0846]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Dollar-led minus own-led follow-through at 1 hour, every slice", "unit": "daily σ", "ref": 0, "note": "95% date-block intervals (regime rows: episode bootstrap; turbulent has 2 episodes, so its interval is not real). Benchmark 0 = no difference; the 1h round trip is 0.037σ. Only NY afternoon clears 0, and the year rows flip sign (2017 +, 2018 -, 2019 +, 2020 -): no stable edge.", "rows": [{"label": "All 7 majors", "value": -0.0006, "lo": -0.0066, "hi": 0.0057}, {"label": "EURUSD", "value": -0.007, "lo": -0.0179, "hi": 0.0041}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "value": -0.0091, "lo": -0.022, "hi": 0.0044}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "value": 0.0018, "lo": -0.0077, "hi": 0.0119}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "value": 0.0103, "lo": -0.0009, "hi": 0.0214}, {"label": "USDCAD", "value": 0.0048, "lo": -0.0062, "hi": 0.0172}, {"label": "USDCHF", "value": 0.0038, "lo": -0.0096, "hi": 0.0169}, {"label": "USDJPY", "value": -0.0002, "lo": -0.0193, "hi": 0.0182}, {"label": "Asia 00-07", "value": -0.0105, "lo": -0.0221, "hi": 0.0021}, {"label": "London open 07-10", "value": -0.0077, "lo": -0.0203, "hi": 0.0046}, {"label": "London mid 10-13", "value": -0.0126, "lo": -0.0255, "hi": 0.0001}, {"label": "Overlap 13-16", "value": -0.0041, "lo": -0.0147, "hi": 0.0069}, {"label": "NY afternoon 16-22", "value": 0.0195, "lo": 0.0061, "hi": 0.0341}, {"label": "Calm regime", "value": 0.0003, "lo": -0.0081, "hi": 0.0111}, {"label": "Turbulent regime", "value": -0.0065, "lo": -0.0184, "hi": 0.0004}, {"label": "σ low third", "value": 0.0009, "lo": -0.0087, "hi": 0.0105}, {"label": "σ mid third", "value": -0.0044, "lo": -0.0128, "hi": 0.0042}, {"label": "σ high third", "value": 0.005, "lo": -0.0047, "hi": 0.0148}, {"label": "2017", "value": 0.0135, "lo": 0.0008, "hi": 0.0277}, {"label": "2018", "value": -0.0105, "lo": -0.0209, "hi": 0.0007}, {"label": "2019", "value": 0.011, "lo": -0.0064, "hi": 0.0272}, {"label": "2020", "value": -0.0137, "lo": -0.0286, "hi": 0.0008}, {"label": "2021", "value": -0.0013, "lo": -0.0155, "hi": 0.0122}, {"label": "2022", "value": -0.0047, "lo": -0.0215, "hi": 0.011}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "To 22:00 London, by time of day: dollar-led and own-led follow-through", "names": ["Dollar-led", "Own-led", "Round-trip spread (cost)"], "unit": "daily σ, signed with the move", "note": "Own-led moves in the NY afternoon give back 0.025σ by 22:00 and dollar-led Asian moves give back 0.07σ; both are smaller than the round trip (spreads widen into 22:00). Benchmark: 0 and the cost bar.", "rows": [{"label": "Asia 00-07", "values": [-0.0738, 0.0091, 0.094]}, {"label": "London open 07-10", "values": [-0.0242, 0.0142, 0.0839]}, {"label": "London mid 10-13", "values": [0.0147, -0.0004, 0.0829]}, {"label": "Overlap 13-16", "values": [-0.0019, 0.0055, 0.0823]}, {"label": "NY afternoon 16-22", "values": [0.0046, -0.0252, 0.0835]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Stop-through: does a fade's stop beyond s·σ get hit within 4 hours?", "names": ["Dollar-led, fade stopped", "Own-led, fade stopped", "Random 15-min boundary (benchmark)"], "unit": "share of moves", "note": "On the M1 bid/ask close path, one spread paid, 4h window cut at 22:00. Dollar-led and own-led stops are hit at the same rate at every stop size; both are hit more often than at a random boundary, because a big move comes with higher vol right then. The follow side's stop is hit at the same rate as the fade's (e.g. 0.59 vs 0.58 at 0.25σ): no direction.", "rows": [{"label": "stop 0.1σ", "values": [0.8366, 0.8313, 0.79]}, {"label": "stop 0.15σ", "values": [0.7461, 0.7462, 0.6734]}, {"label": "stop 0.25σ", "values": [0.5839, 0.5846, 0.4766]}, {"label": "stop 0.4σ", "values": [0.3864, 0.3938, 0.2807]}, {"label": "stop 0.6σ", "values": [0.2153, 0.2276, 0.1352]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "In R: follow or fade a big move, stop = target = 0.25σ, 4 hours", "unit": "R (1R = 0.25σ)", "ref": 0, "note": "First touch on the M1 bid/ask close path (buys at the offer, sells at the bid), else exit at 4h/22:00. Gross = on the mid; net = one spread paid (~0.15R). Benchmark 0. Every net bar is negative, including the one local pattern (NY-afternoon own-led fade).", "rows": [{"label": "Dollar-led follow, gross", "value": -0.0046, "lo": -0.0183, "hi": 0.0098}, {"label": "Own-led follow, gross", "value": -0.0116, "lo": -0.0205, "hi": -0.0025}, {"label": "Dollar-led follow, net", "value": -0.1464, "lo": -0.1625, "hi": -0.1287}, {"label": "Own-led follow, net", "value": -0.1571, "lo": -0.169, "hi": -0.1451}, {"label": "Dollar-led fade, net", "value": -0.1357, "lo": -0.1506, "hi": -0.1217}, {"label": "Own-led fade, net", "value": -0.1346, "lo": -0.1444, "hi": -0.1235}, {"label": "NY afternoon own-led follow, gross", "value": -0.0601, "lo": -0.0768, "hi": -0.0428}, {"label": "NY afternoon own-led fade, net", "value": -0.1182, "lo": -0.1362, "hi": -0.0993}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Correlation vs vol with the Forbes-Rigobon correction", "unit": "mean pairwise correlation (7 majors, 5-min)", "xlabel": "within-year vol decile (same day)", "note": "Corrected = ρ/√(1+δ(1-ρ²)), δ = this decile's variance ÷ the calmest decile's - 1 (mean of the two pairs). 'Forward map' = what pure heteroskedasticity would produce from the calm ρ (the formula printed in Lesson 06; shown as the benchmark, not used as the correction). Observed rises less than the forward map, so the corrected correlation FALLS on loud days: they are own-move days. Sorted by yesterday's vol: corrected 0.41 to 0.32.", "series": [{"name": "Observed", "points": [[1, 0.3952], [2, 0.4153], [3, 0.4459], [4, 0.4586], [5, 0.4681], [6, 0.4659], [7, 0.4962], [8, 0.5137], [9, 0.5382], [10, 0.5046]]}, {"name": "FR-corrected", "points": [[1, 0.3952], [2, 0.3726], [3, 0.376], [4, 0.3719], [5, 0.3624], [6, 0.3444], [7, 0.3517], [8, 0.3452], [9, 0.3338], [10, 0.2318]]}, {"name": "Forward map (pure heteroskedasticity)", "points": 